Q: How chain an order_by() call to a CodeIgniter query built fully by get_where() A: <p>Try this:  </p>

<pre><code>$query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;order_by('topic', 'asc')-&gt;get_where('prepared_forms', array('topic' =&gt; $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('prepared_topics')));
$new_form = $query-&gt;row_array();
</code></pre>

Q: ASP.NET WebForms CustomValidator message not disappearing when checkbox is checked A: <h3>1. Ensure ClientValidationFunction is Set</h3>
<p>Your CustomValidator should have a <code>ClientValidationFunction</code> defined:</p>
<p>aspx</p>
<pre><code>&lt;asp:CustomValidator ID=&quot;cvCheckbox&quot; runat=&quot;server&quot;
    ControlToValidate=&quot;chkAgree&quot;
    ClientValidationFunction=&quot;validateCheckbox&quot;
    ErrorMessage=&quot;You must check the box!&quot;
    Display=&quot;Dynamic&quot;
    ForeColor=&quot;Red&quot;&gt;
&lt;/asp:CustomValidator&gt;

2. Implement the JavaScript Function Correctly
The function must set args.IsValid based on the checkbox state:

javascript
function validateCheckbox(sender, args) {
    var chk = document.getElementById('&lt;%= chkAgree.ClientID %&gt;');
    args.IsValid = chk.checked;
}

3. Trigger Validation on Checkbox Change
By default, validators run when the form is submitted. If you want the error message to disappear immediately when the checkbox is checked, you need to re-validate on change:

javascript
document.getElementById('&lt;%= chkAgree.ClientID %&gt;').onchange = function () {
    ValidatorValidate(document.getElementById('&lt;%= cvCheckbox.ClientID %&gt;'));
};
This forces the CustomValidator to re-check validity when the checkbox state changes.

4. Check ValidationGroup
If you’re using ValidationGroup, make sure the CustomValidator and the submit button belong to the same group. Otherwise, the validator may not behave as expected.
</code></pre>

